{
  "dom_id": "step-q69501",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251309/assets/d32ceace77d77dc5a3b9b1443b0985232ac23837a5cb5b2b5c6969e7cc65bfef.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find $|a|.$",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251309/assets/f2144a9accce690363d34c31ed1c29b4742281eb26c273c91a55776c0ad54e5a.png)\n\nIn $△AHB$ we have $∠AHB={90}^{∘}$, $AH=30\\,\\text{mm}$ and $BH=25\\,\\text{mm}.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\sqrt{A{H}^{2}+B{H}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{30}^{2}+{25}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1\\,525} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{61}\\,\\text{mm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
